My experience with NH/Spork so far has been that players _hate_ instakills
with a passion.  I removed a number of vanilla's and replaced them with
extremely debilitating effects (the "poison was deadly", for example,
now socks you for a big hunk of maxHP instead of killing you outright),
and I've heard nothing but positive remarks from my players about those
changes.

As such, I'm very reluctant to casually include any more instakills,
especially in places where players are used to there _not_ being one.
There are other considerations as well that _aren't_ instakills, but
vanilla has largely been designed about "prayer fixes these troubles
reliably", and as such taking any of that away needs to be carefully
gauged against the positives.  

